u=updates['00254']
u['administration_text']='Swallow the tablet whole with water, with or without food. Do not replace a missed or vomited dose; resume the next scheduled dose.'
u['urgent_extra']='Report persistent limiting joint pain, new tendon pain or swelling, a possible fracture, jaundice or new vaginal bleeding. Sudden loss of tendon function needs prompt assessment. Severe allergic symptoms, chest pain or major breathing difficulty require urgent help.'
u['agents'][0]['explanation']='Anastrozole blocks aromatase, an enzyme that makes oestrogen in fat and other tissues after menopause. Less oestrogen is available to stimulate hormone-sensitive breast cancer cells. This also explains effects such as hot flushes, vaginal dryness and bone thinning. It does not reliably switch off functioning ovaries; any ovarian-suppression treatment needs a separate prescription and checks.'
for q in u['questions']:
    if q['q']=='How long will treatment continue?':q['a']='After early breast cancer treatment, the team sets the intended total endocrine treatment length, taking account of any earlier tamoxifen. A course of several years may later be reviewed for extension according to recurrence risk, tolerance and bone health. Advanced-disease treatment is reviewed according to benefit and tolerance. A review date is not an automatic stop date.'
u['endocrine_timeline']['notes']=[u['administration_text'],'A change from tamoxifen does not automatically restart the whole treatment clock. Ask which earlier treatment counts towards your plan.']

u=updates['00371']
u['purpose']='After surgery, letrozole can reduce the risk of hormone-sensitive breast cancer returning. Before surgery, it can be used in a selected treatment plan to shrink the cancer and prepare for an operation. In advanced disease, the aim is cancer and symptom control. Each setting has its own review and duration plan.'
u['indication_text']='Letrozole is used for selected postmenopausal hormone-sensitive breast cancer before surgery, after surgery, as extended treatment or for advanced disease. Before-surgery treatment also depends on HER2 results, whether chemotherapy is suitable and whether surgery should happen immediately; the team checks these details.'
u['consent_support']='The usual prescription is once daily, but severe liver impairment can require a different frequency. Use the frequency on your prescription and confirm any change with the prescriber or pharmacist. An already reduced or unusual schedule must be reviewed before it is changed. Confirmed menopause is needed for this monotherapy; any ovarian suppression has its own prescription and monitoring.'
u['urgent_extra']='Report new tendon pain or swelling promptly and protect the affected area until assessed; sudden loss of tendon function needs urgent assessment. Also report limiting joint pain, a possible fracture, jaundice or new vaginal bleeding. New breast changes during before-surgery treatment need review rather than waiting for the planned end date. Severe allergic symptoms, chest pain or major breathing difficulty require urgent help.'
u['agents'][0]['explanation']='Letrozole blocks aromatase, reducing the oestrogen made in tissues after menopause and the stimulation of hormone-sensitive breast cancer cells. This can be useful in different settings, but a before-surgery course needs response and surgical reviews, while treatment after surgery has a planned total duration. It does not reliably switch off functioning ovaries; ovarian suppression needs its own treatment plan.'
u['endocrine_timeline']['rows'][0]['label']='Prescribed tablets'
